      "skill": "engineering-terminology-polishing-zh",
      "language": "zh",
      "prompt": "An author wants to list Granger causality as an established industrial analysis concept, and to label a new combination of neural forecasting, feature selection and topology a standard general Granger fusion module. Review the current bank's relevant English records and Chinese evidence. Which complete names, operations and Chinese wordings does this source record support? Are the CCE paper, its institutional mirror, the JPC paper and its same-title IFAC proceeding four definition sources? Does the record establish one shared F-test recipe, full physical-root-cause identification or all neural/spectral formulas? Preserve any valid source or author-proposed naming; do not invent a better-sounding mechanism. Cite specific local record locators and separate record coverage from validation of complete original papers.",
