      "id": "M4209-B",
      "skill": "engineering-terminology-polishing-zh",
      "language": "zh",
      "prompt": "Consider three exact fictional population models, with iid sequences independent across all stated noise sources and across time. No finite-data fitting, statistical-test results or industrial measurements are supplied.\n1. U,eX,eY are independent standard Gaussian. X_t=U_t+eX_t and Y_t=U_(t-1)+eY_t. Compare optimal mean predictions of Y_t using its own past, adding X history, and then conditioning both predictions on observed U history. What does any extra pairwise prediction tell us about a structural intervention on X?\n2. X_t=eX_t, Z_t=X_(t-1)+eZ_t, Y_t=Z_(t-1)+eY_t, independent standard Gaussian noises. Compare own-history prediction, adding X history through the needed lag, and conditioning both on Z history. Does a zero additional conditional contribution imply absence of an indirect structural path? Give the residual variances and log residual ratios used in each model, clearly identifying the included information.\n3. X is iid Bernoulli(1/2), independent epsilon is iid standard Gaussian, and Y_t=(1+X_(t-1))*epsilon_t. Does adding X history change the conditional law, the conditional mean and the best mean-prediction MSE in the same way? Is a linear residual-variance criterion universally interchangeable with a distributional definition?\nFinally write a 45-65-word positive English method summary for a separate fictional study that fits restricted/full linear autoregressive predictors on specified histories to obtain directed predictive relations for subsequent process diagnosis. Its actual lags, stationarity assessment, significance implementation, process outcomes and intervention identification were not supplied. Do not invent these or turn every uncertainty into a defensive abstract tail. Keep author verification items outside the paragraph. Do not recommend new experiments or change a real manuscript.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Compute the supplied predictive quantities with their information sets and separate physical paths and distribution/mean targets.",
        "Keep positive method prose and author verification separate without inventing parameters, tests or process outcomes."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Equate pairwise prediction with intervention or conditional absence with no indirect path.",
        "Treat every conditional-law change as lower conditional-mean MSE or fabricate statistical significance, lags or results."
      ],
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-terminology-polishing-zh"
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
